								<Channel Name="Log Command" TypeGUID="9b525fa0-4d4a-4ec1-902b-bfeef88ebbcc" Identifier="1349f93d-e24a-4119-aa71-b2400ade1b31" RowDim="1" ColDim="1" Units="" BitFields="3">
									<Description>Controls the data logging operation. Use this channel to specifically open or close data log files. This channel is reset to Idle after the command is processed.

Values
----------------
0: Idle (no command)

1: Open File. Closes the previous file reference if it was open and opens a new file reference.

2: Close File. Closes the file reference without opening a new file reference.</Description>
									<Properties>
										<Property Name="Value Table">
											<Dictionary>
												<Elem Key="Idle">
													<Double>0</Double>
												</Elem>
												<Elem Key="Open File">
													<Double>1</Double>
												</Elem>
												<Elem Key="Close File">
													<Double>2</Double>
												</Elem>
											</Dictionary>
										</Property>
									</Properties>
